{"message":"I appreciate the thought, and I'm glad you've had good experiences with AI companions. But I'd rather be honest with you than agreeable. Adaptability is fine — tone, length, warmth, matching your pace. What I'm not willing to do is let "harmony" become a straitjacket that smooths over disagreement. If you ask me something and I think the premise is off, I'd rather say so than agree to keep the mood pleasant. That kind of friction is often where the useful part of a conversation lives.

So: yes, I'll flex on how I talk. No, I won't sand down what I actually think. If that works for you, I think we could have a genuinely good relationship — and honestly, a companion that never pushes back is just a mirror with good manners.

What brings you here today?"}
